<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>

<chapter xml:id="ch_charge-e-fields" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Electric Fields</title>
	<introduction>
    <p> In this chapter you will learn about the fundamental property of charge and electric fields.</p>
	
	</introduction>
		
    <objectives>
      
      <introduction><p>After successful completion of this chapter, you will be able to:</p></introduction>
		<ol>
			<li><p>Describe what charge is and define basic charge properties.</p></li>
			<li><p>Define electric field and electric force.</p></li>
			<li><p>Use forces and Newton's 2nd Law to describe the motion of charges subject to electric forces.</p></li>
			 <li><p>Read and construct electric field vector maps and electric field lines.</p></li>
			<li><p>Determine the electric field due to a single point charge.</p></li>
			<li><p>Determine the electric force between two point charges.</p></li>
		</ol>
	</objectives>

